# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Cloud Build checks the repository out (~14.6 MB tracked) and runs `docker build`. The
# Dockerfile COPYs only backend/, frontend/, coefficient_exploration_output/ and a handful
# of root files — about 1.3 MB. Everything else is packed and transferred for nothing. The
# two big items are the built documentation site and the docs sources: together they are
# roughly 88% of the checkout and neither is served by this container.
#
# Careful: anything the Dockerfile COPYs must NOT be listed here, or the build fails on a
# missing path. Kept deliberately: backend/, frontend/ (minus its build output),
# coefficient_exploration_output/, parameters.yaml, requirements.txt, package.json,
# package-lock.json, tsconfig.json, __init__.py.

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.dockerignore

# ── Documentation: sources and the mkdocs-built site (published to GitHub Pages) ──
docs/
site/
mkdocs.yml
*.md

# ── Tests, tooling, editor and CI config — never part of the runtime image ────────
testing_files/
scripts/
screenshot_review/
.github/
.devcontainer/
.vscode/
.claude/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Local state, caches, credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
.streamlit/
.platform_credentials/
.env
.env.*
*.pem
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage

# ── Built or installed artefacts: the image produces these itself (Dockerfile      ─
#    stage 1 runs npm ci + npm run build, so a stale local dist must not leak in).
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
